      'Setup example: 7 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the last player remaining by avoiding taking zero tricks in any hand; players who take no tricks are knocked out. Win the final one-trick hand or be the sole survivor.',
      "Turn-flow example: Player to dealer's left leads. Must follow suit if able; otherwise any card. Highest trump wins the trick, else highest card of the led suit. Trick winner leads next. A player who takes no tricks is knocked out (first such player gets one dog's life hand of one card). Seven hands per game with 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1 cards dealt respectively.",
      "Scoring example: No points; players are eliminated when they take no tricks in a hand. First such player gets one dog's life; thereafter elimination is immediate. Last player standing wins; or winner of the one trick in the final (one-card) hand..",
